    "title": "UWF announced the passing of football player Ben Conken - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Michael Hanich ,\n22 minutes ago\nVideo above: ‘News 5 Now’ — Top Stories from Aug. 19, 2026\nPENSACOLA, Fla. (WKRG) — The University of West Florida athletics announced the passing of football player Ben Conken after a battle with cancer.\nArmed man in custody after Mobile County standoff, officials say According to an X post from UWF , the former Cottage Hill Christian star was diagnosed with cancer shortly after joining the team.\nHis high school described him as an impact player on and off the field. He was a graduate of the Class of 2024 and chose to continue his football career at the collegiate level with the Argos.\n“Ben was a competitor who gave his all on the football and baseball fields, but he will be remembered for so much more: his easy-going personality, his sense of humor, and his faithfulness as a friend. He was fierce in competition and genuine in friendship,” CHCA said on Facebook .\nMan killed in fiery Mobile County crash Conken’s funeral will be Saturday, Aug. 22, with visitation held from 9:30 a.m. to 11:30 a.m. and the funeral service held afterwards at 11:30 a.m. at Cottage Hill Baptist Church, located at 4255 Cottage Hill Road.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WKRG News 5.",
    "summary": "Video above: ‘News 5 Now’ — Top Stories from Aug. 19, 2026 PENSACOLA, Fla. (WKRG) — The University of West Florida athletics announced the passing of football player Ben Conken after a battle with cancer. Armed man in custody after Mobile County standoff, officials say According to an X post from UWF , the former Cottage Hill Christian star was diagnosed with cancer shortly after joining the team. He was a graduate of the Class of 2024 and chose to continue his football career at the collegiate level with the Argos.",
